Usage: agent-deck update [options]

Check for and install updates (always checks GitHub for latest).

Options:
  -check
    	Only check for updates, don't install
  -check-now
    	Same as --unattended, but for a controller's nudge: checks GitHub right away and never nudges this host's own remotes
  -dry-run
    	With --install-timer/--ensure-timer/--uninstall-timer: print the files and commands, execute nothing
  -ensure-timer
    	Install or heal the update timer only where none is active (what unattended runs, the daemon and remote update do); honours [updates] manage_timer
  -install-timer
    	Install the daily unattended update timer (launchd on macOS, systemd --user on Linux), rewrite a stale one, migrate a legacy agentdeck-autoupdate unit; an active current timer is left alone
  -json
    	With --check: print the result as JSON (current, latest, available, publishing, auto_install, auto_restart, timer, on_disk, running_tuis, pending_launch_agents, remote_nudges); with --timer-status/--install-timer/--ensure-timer: the timer state or what was done
  -timer-status
    	Show whether the daily update timer is installed and loaded (kinds: launchd, systemd, systemd-legacy, none)
  -trigger string
    	Who started this run, for the debug log: tui, timer or manual (default: $AGENTDECK_UPDATE_TRIGGER or manual)
  -unattended
    	Install without prompts (no changelog, no stdin); honours [updates] auto_install; exit 2 on Homebrew installs
  -uninstall-timer
    	Remove the daily unattended update timer
  -version string
    	Install a specific released version (e.g. 1.7.3); may be a downgrade

Examples:
  agent-deck update                     # Check and install latest if available
  agent-deck update --check             # Only check, don't install
  agent-deck update --check --json      # Machine-readable check incl. timer state, running TUIs, pending launch agents
  agent-deck update --version 1.7.3     # Install a specific version (may downgrade)
  agent-deck update --unattended        # No prompts; what the timer and the TUI run
  agent-deck update --check-now          # What a controller's nudge runs on this host
  agent-deck update --install-timer     # Daily unattended update at 07:MM (random minute)
  agent-deck update --install-timer --dry-run
  agent-deck update --ensure-timer      # Install/heal only where no timer is active
  agent-deck update --uninstall-timer
  agent-deck update --timer-status [--json]

On macOS every install re-registers com.agentdeck.* launchd agents that run
this binary (bootout + bootstrap), otherwise they crash-loop with EX_CONFIG.
